WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:05.400
Module 02 · Course 1 · Clarify · For entrepreneurs
Theory of Change

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.800
Explain how your planned work could lead to change: a reasoned hypothesis to test before you launch.

3
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:30.615
This module turns your external objectives into a Theory of Change: a reasoned explanation of how your planned work could lead to lasting change, and which assumptions must hold. It answers: if we do this, why would that change follow?

4
00:00:31.015 --> 00:00:31.615
Why test your logic first

5
00:00:31.615 --> 00:00:38.030
1. Before launch, almost every link between your work and change is an assumption.

6
00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:44.074
2. Naming the critical assumptions shows what to test before you spend money.

7
00:00:44.074 --> 00:00:51.119
3. Funders and partners trust ideas whose reasoning they can follow and question.

8
00:00:51.519 --> 00:01:01.219
What you will work through: 2.1 Understanding Theory of Change · 2.2 Defining the problem · 2.3 Long-term impact · 2.4 Outcomes · 2.5 Outputs · 2.6 Activities · 2.7 Inputs · 2.8 Assumptions, risks and evidence · 2.9 Test, write and use your Theory of Change · 2.10 Recap: Theory of Change

9
00:01:01.619 --> 00:01:02.219
What you will learn to do

10
00:01:02.219 --> 00:01:07.893
1. Describe the problem and its causes, not just the missing solution.

11
00:01:07.893 --> 00:01:13.567
2. Draw one pathway per external objective, from inputs to long-term impact.

12
00:01:13.567 --> 00:01:20.981
3. List the assumptions to test with the people affected, before and after launch.

13
00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:21.981
Practical tips

14
00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:28.396
1. Start from the impact and work backwards; then read it forwards to check.

15
00:01:28.396 --> 00:01:35.181
2. Show a draft to people affected by the problem and ask what is missing.

16
00:01:35.181 --> 00:01:42.596
3. See how our example bakery links paid traineeships to young people’s first jobs.

17
00:01:43.196 --> 00:01:45.196
You create: Your Theory of Change: one pathway per external objective, with its assumptions.

18
00:01:45.196 --> 00:01:49.996
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

19
00:01:51.496 --> 00:01:54.596
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
